# Closed point computations, stated on X.bvalo (values stuck on `one`, never
# expanded): one chunk of the specification's double-and-add loop from a
# literal point to a literal point is one {==} check of the machine of
# ptm.bend (chunk), and the generator G is a point of the group (g_valid).
# The modulus is 1 + X.bvalo(one, p1) for the literals p == p1 + 1 (hn).

def spo(+one: Nat, a: M.BP) -> CS.SPoint:
  match a:
    case M.BP{x, y, z}:
      CS.SPoint{X.bvalo(one, x), X.bvalo(one, y), X.bvalo(one, z)}

